  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 110 AM CDT Tue Jul 28 2026\n\nNorthwest flow will continue through the end of the week. A \ndisturbance on Thursday will bring a chance for showers and \nthunderstorms throughout the day. The Upper level ridge then \nbegins to build back in from the west pushing the northwest flow\neastward with the ridge becoming centered over the central \nCONUS. WAA increases to the region by the latter half of the \nweekend and will start to see a return to hot temperatures with \nhighs reaching mid 90s Sunday and Monday. At this time although \nthere will be hotter temperatures and low level moisture does \nincrease, heat indicies will still remain below any heat \nheadline criteria. Will need to continue to monitor as we get \ncloser to the weekend into early next week. \n\nAs far as precipitation potential for the end of the week into \nthe weekend, at this time expect mostly dry conditions, Friday \nthrough Sunday as the region remains under the upper level ridge.\nAs for fire weather concerns, it will remain low through the \nend of the week, then will need to monitor heading into the \nweekend as dry conditions move in with warmer temperatures.",
